?>
<!-- User Dashboard & Access Section -->
<div class="card">
	<h3 id="feature-user-dashboard" class="ffc-icon-user"><?php esc_html_e( 'User Dashboard & Access', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></h3>
	<p><?php esc_html_e( 'A front-end panel where each logged-in user sees their own data — issued certificates, appointments and profile — without any admin access.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>

	<div class="ffc-doc-example">
		<h4><?php esc_html_e( 'Adding the dashboard', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></h4>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'Place the shortcode on any page (for example a "My Account" page):', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<pre><code>[user_dashboard_personal]</code></pre>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The page is excluded from full-page caching automatically, because it renders user-specific data that must never be served from a shared cache.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
	</div>

	<div class="ffc-doc-example">
		<h4><?php esc_html_e( 'What the user sees', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></h4>
		<ul>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'Their own issued certificates, with download / verification links', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'Their personal-calendar appointments (with receipt / cancel actions where allowed)', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'A waitlisted appointment is labelled Waitlisted and offers Leave waitlist; an open one that can no longer be cancelled says why, the calendar taking no online cancellations or the deadline having passed. An administrator is held to the calendar\'s admin bypass switch here as on the cancellation itself.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'The reregistration banner and "Download Record" action when a reregistration applies to them', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'View answers on a reregistration they sent, which opens their answers under the row even after the campaign closed. CPF, RF, RG, phones, e-mails and the birth date arrive masked behind a Reveal button; viewing as a user, the reveal is recorded in the activity log.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'Their audience bookings, and the Recruitment tab with their call-ups, when they belong to an audience or are linked to a candidate', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'A post-event certificate form still waiting for them: the booking shows Fill in the form, their personal link, and when the form closes, and a notice at the top of the tab counts the forms waiting. Viewing as a user shows that a form waits, never its link.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'A Profile tab, read from the plugin\'s own user profile, where they edit their display name, phone, department, organization, notes and birth date (stored encrypted, and the date Date Messages uses)', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'Notification Preferences on the Profile tab: an "Appointment reminder" toggle, on until turned off', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'A Messages tab, when the Date Messages module is on: what the module sent them, in two groups that page three at a time. Current holds the announcements sent within the days chosen on Date Messages → Settings, and the tab shows how many; Earlier holds the date messages and the older announcements. Each message opens in place with Open and closes with Close, and is marked as also sent by e-mail. Beside the list, Message preferences holds the "Date messages" and "Announcements from this site" toggles, each of which opts them out, on until turned off.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'The current announcements also open the dashboard as notices above the cards, at most three, each with "Read in Messages". A notice has no close button: it leaves when its days are over, and it is not shown to someone who turned announcements off, although the announcement stays in their Messages tab.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'A message is built again from its rule each time the tab is read, so an edited rule shows its current text and a deleted rule leaves the tab. What a disabled rule sent stays, unless Date Messages → Settings hides it. A send that failed is not listed, and the delivery log, and so the tab, keeps one year. Viewing as a user, the e-mail address and the values the date supplies, such as an age, are masked, and the unsubscribe link in a message leads to the tab\'s preferences.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><?php esc_html_e( 'Change Password, and Privacy & Data (LGPD) buttons to request an export or the deletion of their personal data', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
		</ul>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The Certificates tab lists each certificate with its form, issue date, consent, e-mail, authentication code and a Download PDF button where the account may download. The From and To dates filter by the day the certificate was issued, in the site\'s timezone, and the search matches the form name and the code. The e-mail shows only as a placeholder until Reveal is pressed. Without the certificate history capability only the most recent certificate of each form is listed, and the Certificates card at the top counts the same certificates the tab lists.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'A tab appears only when the account holds its capability and its module is switched on in Settings → Modules; a link to a tab the account does not have opens the first tab it does have. A filter that matches nothing says so, with a button to clear it. When the session expires, the dashboard says so once, with a button to reload the page, and the browser\'s Back button returns to the previous tab.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The personal-calendar and group-calendar tabs split the list into Upcoming, Past and Cancelled, each heading showing how many items it holds. Each section pages on its own, 5 upcoming, 3 past and 2 cancelled items at a time, and the filter bar brings every section back to its first page.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The Recruitment tab, My Calls, sorts the candidate\'s classifications by status, with a counter for each at the top. Called holds one card per active call, with the presentation date and time, how many days away it is and an "Add to calendar" button that downloads an .ics file. Waiting lists final classifications first and then preliminary ones, 5 rows at a time. Closed lists hired, withdrew, did not show up and "Deadline passed", 2 rows at a time. A call still marked as called moves from Called to Closed as "Deadline passed" the day after its presentation date, in the site\'s timezone, until the team records the result. An i button beside a badge explains a passed deadline or a reverted call, with its dates and the reason given. An empty section is not shown.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'Closed shows each row\'s position and score, as Waiting does. When a notice is closed, its rows leave Called and Waiting and are listed under Closed. A row with no result yet reads "Notice closed"; a recorded result or a passed deadline keeps its own badge. Only the label changes: the candidate\'s status in the notice stays as it was.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'With the Site PWA plugin installed, the dashboard also appears inside its installable app, one screen per part: Agenda (personal appointments and audience bookings), Presence, raised in the middle of the bar, and Certificates in the bottom navigation, and Messages, Reregistration, Recruitment and Profile under More. Each screen appears only to an account that has the matching tab. On the phone where the account\'s presence is active, the app also lists Pair terminal and My terminals to holders of ffc_manage_audiences_terminals, and Operator QR to holders of ffc_checkin_audiences; on any other phone, and until presence is activated, they stay out of More. Manual attendance, for holders of ffc_checkin_audiences, opens Audience Bookings in wp-admin. Without Site PWA nothing changes.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'Certificates in the app is its own screen rather than the dashboard table: a search by course or code, the newest certificate as a card (marked New for its first 7 days) with Open PDF, and the others as rows that open their PDF. It reads the same list as the dashboard, so downloading follows the same permissions.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'In the app\'s bottom bar, Certificates shows how many certificates were issued since the person last opened that screen, counting the last 7 days at most and up to 9+; opening the screen clears it.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'Agenda in the app is its own screen rather than the dashboard tables: My bookings shows one card per day, today highlighted, with the status or the attendance as a chip and the next step inline (the presence code for an event, its post-event form, an appointment\'s receipt); what already took place folds into one group. Book lists the personal calendars that a published page lets the person book; a calendar opens inside the app when Site PWA can draw its page, and on the site otherwise. It reads the same lists as the dashboard.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'On the day of a certificate form the event terminal reads, Agenda also shows it as Certificate on the spot, with its hours and Show my QR; a form that asks for a ticket says to have the code ready, a form with a consent field says that showing the QR accepts it, with a link to the full terms, and a form whose certificate was issued shows Certificate issued.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'Once the terminal has read the QR, the card leads to Certificates: a reading that waits on profile data shows To complete with Complete in Certificates, where the missing data is filled in, and an issued certificate shows View in Certificates. The same reading appears under Pending on Home.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'The app\'s Home shows what the plugin knows is next for the person: "Attendance confirmed at" an event recorded in the last 7 days, as a line they can dismiss; their next booking in the coming 7 days, with Presence QR and Details; and, under Pending, each post-event form still open, each reregistration they can still submit with its deadline, and a certificate issued in the last 7 days. Each item opens the matching screen, and one the account cannot open is left out.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'The app\'s More screen opens on the person, with their RF masked and their department under their name, and lists the operator screens apart, under Operator, each with a line saying what it is for; My terminals shows how many of the terminals the operator paired are active and how many of those are offline, and Reregistration shows Pending while a campaign is still open for them. Turning the app\'s dark theme on for one device also turns the plugin\'s screens inside the app dark, whatever Dark Mode says. In the light theme the plugin\'s screens inside the app take the app\'s accent colour and corners, set in the Site PWA plugin, with the text on the accent in the contrasting colour the app computes.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'In the app, the notification toggles are on the Preferences screen, in a Notifications section: "Appointment reminder", plus "Date messages" and "Announcements from this site" for an account that has the Messages tab. The app\'s Profile and Messages screens leave them out.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'The app locks with the phone\'s own screen lock (fingerprint, face or the phone\'s PIN) when it opens and when it comes back after a few seconds away; for holders of ffc_checkin_audiences or ffc_manage_audiences_terminals the lock is mandatory, so the app shows nothing until it is turned on, and everyone else is invited to turn it on.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The dashboard is drawn with the plugin\'s own palette and icons, so it follows Dark Mode, and its fields, buttons and status badges look like those of the public forms. With Public Design switched on it also takes the design\'s font, accent colour, field corners and card corners.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <a href="#config-public-design"><?php esc_html_e( 'Public Design', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></a></p>
	</div>

	<div class="ffc-doc-example">
		<h4><?php esc_html_e( 'Access control', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></h4>
		<ul>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'Must be logged in:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'the dashboard resolves data from the current user and shows nothing to anonymous visitors.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'Own data only:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'records are matched to the current user (and their CPF/RF); a user never sees another user\'s data.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'Masked personal data:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'the person\'s own CPF/RF, e-mail addresses, phone and birth date appear masked on every tab, each with a Reveal button, so a shared or projected screen does not show them. Revealing one\'s own data writes no activity-log entry, and a masked field cannot be saved over until it is revealed. Documents the person downloads (a certificate PDF, a receipt, a record) keep printing the values in clear.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'View as user:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'holders of ffc_view_as_user can open the dashboard as another user, under a banner, from the users list or the user-edit screen ("View as user", which opens a new tab; the users list shows the column only to holders of ffc_view_as_user). The other user\'s personal data appears masked, as it does to its owner, and each Reveal there writes an activity-log entry.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'Viewing as someone needs ffc_view_as_user and permission to edit that account in wp-admin, for the page and for every request it makes. The password cannot be changed while viewing as another account, and an expired or invalid link shows a notice instead of a dashboard.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'Nor can a privacy request be made there, since it is the data subject\'s own, and a profile edit made while viewing as someone is logged under the account that made it, naming the account edited.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'Password-set link:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'the link in an invitation e-mail opens the dashboard\'s password screen and lasts seven days unless the reregistration settings say otherwise. The key leaves the address bar on the first visit and is kept in a short-lived cookie the page\'s scripts cannot read, so it is not left in the browser history or sent to other sites. The change-password form links to WordPress\'s own "Lost your password?" for a member who no longer knows the current one.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?> <?php esc_html_e( 'A link that has expired or was already used opens the login notice with a message saying so and a button to ask for a new password.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'Staff accounts:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'a staff account — a WordPress administrator, FFC Administrator, any module role from Operator up, or an account that can reveal personal data or manage a module — never receives a password-set link, and a link issued before it became one stops working: such an account resets its password through WordPress. When an import or a form matches a staff account by e-mail, the record is linked to it but its name, profile data and roles are left as they are.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
			<li><strong><?php esc_html_e( 'Roles & capabilities:', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></strong> <?php esc_html_e( 'admin surfaces are gated separately by FFC capabilities — see the Capabilities & Roles reference page.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></li>
		</ul>
	</div>

	<div class="ffc-doc-example">
		<h4><?php esc_html_e( 'Profile custom fields', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></h4>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The identity/contact/address/employment fields live on the plugin\'s user profile and are mapped to the reregistration and audience data, so a user\'s details stay consistent across a certificate PDF, a record and their profile. WordPress\'s first and last name follow the plugin\'s full name (first word / the rest), and editing First/Last Name on the user-edit screen updates it back.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'Administrators see and edit the same fields on the user-edit screen, in the "FFC Custom Data" section, grouped by the audiences the user belongs to. They behave as on the reregistration form: CPF, RF, RG and phone fields are masked and validated, dependent selects follow their parent, and a field mapped to the profile is saved there, encrypted when it holds personal data, so the profile, the dashboard and the next reregistration read the same value.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
		<p><?php esc_html_e( 'The user sees the same fields on the dashboard\'s Profile tab, on the site and in the app, one section per audience, and edits them under Edit Profile with the reregistration form\'s controls. A sensitive value is masked until revealed, an invalid value refuses the save with a message under the field, and an empty required field keeps its stored value. CPF and RF are shown but changed only by an administrator, and a field mapped to the name, phone, department, organization, notes or birth date is edited with the profile fields above it.', 'ffcertificate' ); ?></p>
	</div>
</div>
